# CSS File Explanation — Flask Search UI

## Overview
This CSS file styles a minimal search interface for a Flask web application. It includes:
- A centered layout
- A search label
- A search input + search button (same row)
- Three action buttons (Add / Remove / Process)
- Dark blue theme
- Monospace font (Source Code Pro)

The layout is built primarily using Flexbox.

---

## 1. Font Import

@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Source+Code+Pro:wght@400;600&display=swap');

- Imports the Source Code Pro font from Google Fonts
- Provides a monospace, developer-style appearance

---

## 2. Page Reset

html, body {
    height: 100%;
    margin: 0;
}

- Removes default browser margins
- Ensures full viewport height is available for centering

---

## 3. Main Layout (Centering System)

body {
    min-height: 100vh;
    background-color: #2F578A;

    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;

    font-family: 'Source Code Pro', monospace;

    transform: translateY(-60px);
}

### Explanation
- `background-color`: sets dark blue theme
- `display: flex`: enables Flexbox layout
- `justify-content: center`: centers horizontally
- `align-items: center`: centers vertically
- `font-family`: applies monospace font globally
- `transform: translateY(-60px)`: moves UI slightly upward for better visual balance

---

## 4. Form Layout (Vertical Stack)

#search_form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
}

### Explanation
- Stacks elements vertically:
  1. Label
  2. Search row
  3. Action buttons row
- Centers everything horizontally inside the form

---

## 5. Label Styling

#search_form label {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    color: white;
    font-size: 16px;
    text-align: center;
}

- Adds spacing below label
- White text for contrast
- Center aligned

---

## 6. Search Row (Input + Button)

.search-row {
    display: flex;
}

### Result Layout
[ search input ] [ search button ]

- Places input and button on same row using Flexbox

---

## 7. Search Input

#search_input {
    width: 210px;
    padding: 8px;
    border: none;
    outline: none;
    border-radius: 10px 0 0 10px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-family: inherit;
}

- Fixed width input
- No border or outline for clean UI
- Rounded left corners only
- Inherits global font

---

## 8. Search Button

.search-row button {
    padding: 8px 12px;
    border: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    background: #1f3f66;
    color: white;
    border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-family: inherit;
}

.search-row button:hover {
    background: #16314f;
}

- Dark blue button matching theme
- Rounded right corners to complete search bar shape
- Hover effect darkens button for feedback

---

## 9. Action Buttons Row

.action-row {
    display: flex;
    margin-top: 10px;
    width: 100%;
    gap: 8px;
}

- Creates horizontal row for Add / Remove / Process buttons
- `gap` adds spacing between buttons
- `margin-top` separates from search bar

---

## 10. Action Buttons

.action-row button {
    flex: 1;
    padding: 7px;
    border: none;
    cursor: pointer;

    background: #1f3f66;
    color: white;

    font-size: 12px;
    font-family: inherit;

    border-radius: 8px;
}

.action-row button:hover {
    background: #16314f;
}

### Explanation
- `flex: 1` → makes all buttons equal width
- Compact padding for smaller UI
- Rounded corners for modern look
- Same color system as search button
- Hover effect improves interactivity

---

## Final UI Structure

           Search By

      [ search input ][ search ]

   [ Add ] [ Remove ] [ Process ]

---

## Key Concepts Used
- Flexbox centering (page layout)
- Column stacking (form structure)
- Row layouts (input + buttons)
- Equal width buttons (`flex: 1`)
- Visual adjustment (`translateY`)
- Consistent design system (color, font, spacing)